1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,536
In this lesson, you'll learn to run your
diary day to day: booking appointments by

2
00:00:05,536 --> 00:00:09,712
hand, rescheduling, cancelling, and
keeping every status up to date,

3
00:00:09,712 --> 00:00:10,879
including no-shows.

4
00:00:11,753 --> 00:00:13,418
This is the Calendar View.

5
00:00:13,418 --> 00:00:16,940
Each block is an appointment,
coloured by its calendar,

6
00:00:16,940 --> 00:00:19,373
so you can read your week at a glance.

7
00:00:19,373 --> 00:00:23,215
The dot in the corner shows the
status: green for confirmed,

8
00:00:23,215 --> 00:00:26,161
orange for unconfirmed,
and red for a no-show.

9
00:00:27,213 --> 00:00:30,179
Switch between day, week
and month at the top.

10
00:00:30,179 --> 00:00:33,468
On the right, filter by
calendar or by team member.

11
00:00:33,468 --> 00:00:37,595
Untick James, and you only see
Sarah's and Priya's appointments.

12
00:00:37,595 --> 00:00:39,788
Tick him again to bring them back.

13
00:00:39,788 --> 00:00:44,431
Filters are handy for front-desk staff
who manage one clinician's diary.

14
00:00:45,282 --> 00:00:50,631
Most patients book online, but when someone
phones or messages, book it yourself.

15
00:00:50,631 --> 00:00:54,462
Olivia asked for Thursday, so
click New, then Appointment.

16
00:00:54,462 --> 00:00:59,811
Booking by hand works just like online
booking: confirmations and reminders still

17
00:00:59,811 --> 00:01:00,273
go out.

18
00:01:01,123 --> 00:01:03,861
Choose the calendar,
search for the contact,

19
00:01:03,861 --> 00:01:06,599
then pick the day and
one of the free times.

20
00:01:06,599 --> 00:01:09,897
Kyntlo only shows slots that
are genuinely available.

21
00:01:09,897 --> 00:01:14,315
Click Book appointment, and Olivia
gets her confirmation automatically.

22
00:01:15,166 --> 00:01:19,616
Click any appointment to open its
details: who it's with, when and where,

23
00:01:19,616 --> 00:01:24,310
the patient's contact details, and the
full history of what's happened to it.

24
00:01:24,310 --> 00:01:27,968
You can also add internal notes
that only your team can see.

25
00:01:28,817 --> 00:01:30,989
Liam can't make Tuesday any more.

26
00:01:30,989 --> 00:01:34,742
Click Reschedule, pick the
new day and time, and confirm.

27
00:01:34,742 --> 00:01:39,416
Liam is notified automatically, and
his calendar invite is updated too.

28
00:01:39,416 --> 00:01:41,851
There's no need to cancel and rebook.

29
00:01:42,704 --> 00:01:45,810
The status tells everyone
what actually happened.

30
00:01:45,810 --> 00:01:50,564
Daniel came in for his check-up, so
open his appointment, click the status,

31
00:01:50,564 --> 00:01:51,705
and choose Showed.

32
00:01:51,705 --> 00:01:55,444
Your reports, and your automations,
rely on these statuses,

33
00:01:55,444 --> 00:01:58,106
including the show rate on your dashboard.

34
00:01:58,956 --> 00:02:03,510
If a patient doesn't turn up, open the
appointment and click Mark no-show.

35
00:02:03,510 --> 00:02:06,771
It's striped in red on the
calendar, and in Module 9,

36
00:02:06,771 --> 00:02:10,525
you'll send a friendly re-booking
text whenever this happens.

37
00:02:11,374 --> 00:02:14,448
To cancel, open the
appointment and click Cancel.

38
00:02:14,448 --> 00:02:17,146
The time opens up again
for other patients,

39
00:02:17,146 --> 00:02:20,158
and the patient receives
a cancellation message.

40
00:02:20,158 --> 00:02:23,483
If you'd rather keep the
patient, reschedule instead,

41
00:02:23,483 --> 00:02:26,307
so the booking and its
history stay together.

42
00:02:27,156 --> 00:02:28,054
Prefer a list?

43
00:02:28,054 --> 00:02:31,647
The Appointment List tab shows
every booking in a table.

44
00:02:31,647 --> 00:02:36,331
Switch between upcoming and cancelled,
filter by calendar or team member,

45
00:02:36,331 --> 00:02:38,384
or search for a patient by name.

46
00:02:39,234 --> 00:02:40,268
Here's a pro tip.

47
00:02:40,268 --> 00:02:44,405
At the end of each day, mark every
appointment as Showed or No-show.

48
00:02:44,405 --> 00:02:47,995
It takes two minutes, and it
powers your show-rate reports,

49
00:02:47,995 --> 00:02:51,037
your no-show follow-ups,
and your review requests.

50
00:02:51,892 --> 00:02:53,665
Your diary is under control!

51
00:02:53,665 --> 00:02:58,667
In the next lesson, we'll cut no-shows
with automatic email and text reminders.

52
00:02:58,667 --> 00:02:59,553
See you there.
